  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/170) by Paul Matthijsse (Bitbucket: [Paul Matthijsse](https://bitbucket.org/Paul Matthijsse), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nHello Alberto, this is a proposal to make the Spot removal tool easier to use, especially for removing lots of dust spots on eg. scanned negatives. I propose to add a “simple mode”, the only slider needed is the size slider. Now activate the tool and click the Add/Edit button to start working. Press Ctrl and the size of the circle is shown, use the size slider to adapt to taste. Next: Ctrl\\+click sets the area next to the spot, but without showing the circles \\(they’re a bit distracting\\). Then paint with the mouse over the spot to be removed. Ctrl\\+click again for the next spot. \n\nThis is how the Repair tool in Gimp works and it is really much more convenient - and faster - to clean up negatives. The technology needed is already available in your tool, so I essentially propose to enrich the interface with this added “simple mode” \\(or retouch mode or scan mode\\). \n\nRegards, Paul.\n",
